+```markdown
+# Complexity Analysis for Problem X
+
+## Constraints
+- N ≤ 1e5
+- Each value ≤ 1e9
+- Time limit: 1 second
+
+## Operation Budget
+- Python can do ~1e8 simple operations per second
+- For 1-second limit: budget = 1e8 operations
+- For N=1e5: max complexity is O(N log N) ~ 1.7e6 ops ✓
+- O(N^2) would be 1e10 ops ✗ (too slow)
+
+## Chosen Algorithm
+- Sliding window with monotonic deque
+- Complexity: O(N) - each element processed once
+- Fits budget ✓
+
+## Critical Bans
+- No floating-point for large integers (using integer division)
+- No exponential search (N! would be huge)
+```
